  "theorem_name": "PrimitiveWordReductionAndMonotoneValuationExclusion",
  "declared_proposition": "If u has affine cycle data (B,D) and w=u^r, then D(w)=D(u)Q_r and B(w)=B(u)Q_r for the same positive geometric factor Q_r; hence D(w) divides B(w) exactly when D(u) divides B(u). In addition, a positive accelerated cycle whose valuations all satisfy v_j>=2 is only the fixed point n=1 with constant word (2,...,2). Therefore every nontrivial cycle candidate reduces to a primitive contracting word containing valuation one.",
  "mathematical_argument": "The affine map of u is F(n)=(3^h n+B)/2^S. Iterating F r times factors both 2^(rS)-3^(rh) and B(u^r) by the same geometric sum, which proves primitive-root equivalence. If every v_j>=2, then T(n)=(3n+1)/2^v is strictly smaller than n for every odd n>1. A positive cycle is therefore impossible unless it reaches n=1, where the exact valuation is two and the orbit stays fixed.",
